00:06:40,909 --> 00:06:46,909
Let the festivities begin.

2
00:13:21,818 --> 00:13:27,818
Midsommar is a horror, drama, mystery film directed by Ari Aster.

3
00:20:02,727 --> 00:20:08,727
Several friends travel to Sweden to study as anthropologists a summer festival that
is held every ninety years in the remote hometown of one of them.

4
00:26:43,636 --> 00:26:49,636
What begins as a dream vacation in a place where the sun never sets, gradually turns into a dark nightmare as
the mysterious inhabitants invite them to participate in their disturbing festive activities.

5
00:33:24,545 --> 00:33:30,545
Dani, played by Florence Pugh.

6
00:40:05,454 --> 00:40:11,454
Christian, played by Jack Reynor.

7
00:46:46,363 --> 00:46:52,363
Josh, played by William Jackson Harper.

8
00:53:27,272 --> 00:53:33,272
Mark, played by Will Poulter.

9
01:00:08,181 --> 01:00:14,181
Pelle, played by Vilhelm Blomgren.

10
01:06:49,090 --> 01:06:55,090
Maja, played by Isabelle Grill.

11
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Midsommar is a 2019 folk horror film written and directed by Ari Aster.

12
01:20:10,909 --> 01:20:16,909
It stars Florence Pugh and Jack Reynor as an American couple who
are drawn into a violent cult in rural Sweden.

13
01:26:51,818 --> 01:26:57,818
Supporting actors include William Jackson Harper, Vilhelm Blomgren,
Ellora Torchia, Archie Madekwe, and Will Poulter.

14
01:33:32,727 --> 01:33:38,727
A co-production between the United States and Sweden, Midsommar was initially pitched
to Aster as a straightforward slasher film set among Swedish cultists.

15
01:40:13,636 --> 01:40:19,636
While elements of the original concept remain in the final product, the finished film focuses on a
deteriorating relationship inspired by a difficult breakup experienced by Aster himself.

16
01:46:54,545 --> 01:47:00,545
The film's soundtrack, composed by the British electronic musician
Bobby Krlic, takes inspiration from Nordic folk music.

17
01:53:35,454 --> 01:53:41,454
The film was predominantly shot on location within the Budapest
metropolitan area of Hungary, from July to October 2018.

18
02:00:16,363 --> 02:00:22,363
Midsommar was theatrically released in the United States by A24 on July
3, 2019, and in Sweden by Nordisk Film on July 10, 2019.

19
02:06:57,272 --> 02:07:03,272
The film grossed $48 million and received positive reviews, with
praise for Aster's direction and Pugh's performance.

20
02:13:38,181 --> 02:13:44,181
The film explores themes of loss of loved one, ritual, paranoia, sweden, cult.

21
02:20:19,090 --> 02:20:25,090
The tone is dark and emotional and mind_bending.
